{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112101,"nonce":"OLbJouBpfULZgG9/+3Gp9M9mVHA=","title":"1.3 Time control: advance-until, tps throttle","message":"Wave 1 — substrate. Depends: 1.1, 1.2 (event-match halting), 0.1 findings.\n\n## Goal\nTurn-based time: paused by default, advance deliberately, halt on what\nmatters, never cook the laptop.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Time model\n- decompiled `TickManager.cs` (TickManagerUpdate, DoSingleTick,\n  TickRateMultiplier, UltraSpeedBoost)\n- 0.1 FINDINGS.md (per-frame update set, tps table, thermal cap)\n- MP catch-up loop (reference for correct fast-forward)\n\n## Scope\n- Verbs: `pause`, `unpause {speed}`, `advance {ticks | until, max_tps,\n  timeout_ticks}` where until ::= {letter[:def] | alert[:id] | event:{type,\n  filter} | any-letter | any-threat}. Halt reasons returned: {reason, tick,\n  ticks_elapsed, journal_seq_range}.\n- Implementation: budgeted DoSingleTick loop inside the frame callback,\n  honoring the 0.1 per-frame update set; duty cycle derived from max_tps;\n  hard cap from config regardless of caller.\n- Own the pause: vanilla forced-pause letters must not leave time running or\n  fight the driver; advance ALWAYS returns paused.\n- Optional halt-on-red-error flag (default on).\n\n## Invariants\nadvance returns paused, always, including on timeout/exception; thermal cap\nis enforced server-side; halting is journal-consistent (events up to the halt\ntick are flushed before the result is written).\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nuntil-condition surface for v1 (keep minimal: journal-event matchers; defer a\npredicate language); interaction with modal windows that pause; whether\nvanilla speeds are used at all vs always the own loop.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `advance ticks:60000` halts at exactly +60000 paused.\n- `advance until:letter` with a dev-triggered raid halts within one tick of\n  the letter, reason=letter, journal contains it.\n- Sustained advance holds ≤ configured max_tps (measured over 5+ min) and\n  a deliberately absurd request still respects the hard cap.\n- Timeout path returns reason=timeout, paused.","files":null}]}